                        \\\
                        {}^{\mathllap{e' g}}\downarrow &amp; &amp;
                        \\downarrow^{\mathrlap{e'}}
                        \\\
                        a' &amp;\underset{Id}{\to}&amp; a'
                        }
                        \\,.
                %p
                  The codomain and domain do match, since
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi f
                        %mi e
                        %mo =
                        %mi e
                        %mo ′
                        %mi g
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f e = e' g
                  by the existence of the original morphism, and their composite is the original morphism
                .maruku-equation
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mrow
                          %mtable
